7592186483307 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483307 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483307 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186482886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483307 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b0979245-762e-5229-aacd-89b1d72de194" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482882 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186482826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483320 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cbc02d96-2205-5f54-a299-6c4d0c2021ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186482916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483328 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "df59866d-4c1e-5c2c-a658-0b6f4acd9b56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-4}} both sides of the equation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f885aae-2228-5978-9940-05380822e48d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483355 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186497486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Systems of ODEs Using Variation of Parameters" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186497449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496656 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b003c2d7-68ae-5238-bc0