237 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497237 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497237 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186497060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497237 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2e897fb2-9841-5b9d-a780-0a38ba920dc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497292 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186496717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497292 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497292 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497292 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186496717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497292 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9bbf6a85-16be-5ce4-a166-d683ed32df25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186497232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186497237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497352 #edb/ref 1069 "q-337102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497352 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497352 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}},\\,Φ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2{e}^{3t}$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{10}{3}$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186497352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3cbf4a14-013f-525c-b169-07b2a7a14f29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497352 #edb/ref 1074 "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-3t}{e}^{t}-0\\cdot {e}^{t}}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}. \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int -2{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 4{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-2}{3}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-2}{3}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}. \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{10}{3} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186497428 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497428 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "263c0b72-c299-51ac-98e0-f88dd4d823d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497428 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497449 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497449 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c983da7-ca72-5a73-bf3a-e7f56ec9519d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497449 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497452 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497452 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "842ea0d1-eabb-5f2a-bca0-30802bda115c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497452 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186365792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497458 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186497486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497458 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "98dc1837-552f-563e-a960-0f664d971bb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497458 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186497352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497486 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fc7dda2f-cd2a-50cf-8f0a-dcfa59501811" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497486 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186497377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186515692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514852 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514852 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Systems of ODEs Using Variation of Pa